# Donor identity — per branch (D-38 clarified 2026-08-16)

**Founder lock.** Donors exist to **avoid designing from scratch**. Use each donor’s **look, layout, screens, and features**; customise copy/branding for DIAL; **wire every action to DIAL APIs**.

## Hard ban — shared DIAL visual identity across branches

- **Do NOT** invent or enforce one shared DIAL brand / `AppShell` look for Spare, Tech, Grocery, Supplier, Delivery, Account.
- Shared chrome (`AppShell`, global design-tokens as a single storefront skin) is **wrong** for cross-branch customer UX.
- Each branch keeps a **distinct visual identity from its locked donor**.

## Branch → donor map

| Branch | Donor | Expectation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Dial a Tech (`/tech`, tech native) | [`AyanSujon/FixItNow`](https://github.com/AyanSujon/FixItNow) | Selecting Dial a Tech lands on a surface that **reads as FixItNow** (orange home-services marketplace), not the shared DIAL shell |
| Spare | Mercur B2C | Mercur B2C storefront patterns |
| Supplier | Mercur vendor-panel | Vendor-panel patterns |
| Grocery | Marketplace / food patterns (Pack) | Donor marketplace patterns |
| Natives | Pack §9 donors | Per-platform donor UX |

Secondary Tech references (NearServe, Homezy) stay companions only — FixItNow is primary.

## Still locked (unchanged)

- Never adopt donor **backends / ledgers / auth / payments** as SoR.
- Money = DIAL packages (`amountMinor`, outbox, Job Reserve).
- Official WhatsApp Cloud API only; MapLibre SoR; agency (D-58).
- No live payment / WhatsApp / tax keys until production-ready (`dial-credentials-after-testing.mdc`).
- Prefer **pattern recreation** when donor LICENSE is missing or unclear — do not vendor donor **backend** source trees wholesale.
- **Founder override (2026-08-16) — FixItNow UI only:** copy the **customer-facing Next.js UI** (pages, layouts, components, CSS/Tailwind/shadcn, public assets) into Dial a Tech. Do **not** treat donor Mongo/Stripe/SSLCommerz/JWT/auth as SoR. Do **not** paste donor git history or `node_modules`. Still no Baileys / unofficial WA; still no Expo.

## Eng obligations

- Prefer **branch-scoped** components/CSS (e.g. `app/tech/tech.css`, `.fin-tech`) over global shell reuse across branches. Tech may use copied FixItNow `components/ui` + `components/common` as long as Tailwind tokens stay under `.fin-tech`.
- Thin vertical OK for large rebuilds: donor-looking landing + one critical path wired to real DIAL APIs — **not** stubs-as-MVP.
- ENH-609 tracks **per-branch donor rebuilds**, not a shared branding programme.
- **Plan SoR:** `docs/planning/DIAL_Donor_Parity_Roadmap.md` (screen matrices, waves, DoD, licence). Do not claim donor parity from a thin vertical.

